[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2605261115-makura-foam-pillow-tier-b-actor-r0", :adr/title "ADR-2605261115: makura (枕) — Foam Pillow Manufacturing Tier-B Actor R0 Scaffold", :adr/status "proposed", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2605261115: makura (枕) — Foam Pillow Manufacturing Tier-B Actor R0 Scaffold\n\n**Status**: proposed\n**Date**: 2026-05-25\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (author), Council Lv6+ (ratify)\n**ADR Hierarchy**: Sibling of ADR-2605242000 (wadachi), ADR-2605250500 (yakushi), ADR-2605250715 (tatekata), ADR-2605252200 (watatsumi), ADR-2605261015 (mitsuho), ADR-2605261030 (hagukumi). Parent constitutional: ADR-2605192100 §1.13 (Wellbecoming applied to sleep/rest) + ADR-2605192200 §2(e) (anti-gatekeeping of basic comfort goods).\n\n## Context\n\nSleep is a foundational Wellbecoming domain (ADR-2605192100 §1.13). Pillows — the most consumed domestic comfort article after textiles themselves — are dominated globally by a few brand-licensors that capture margin via licensed character IP, fragrance/aromatherapy add-ons, smart-IoT sensor packages, and OEM-opaque chemistry. The underlying manufacturing methodology — polyurethane (PU) foam slabstock blowing, mechanical shredding to crumb, woven shell sewing, pneumatic crumb filling, and vacuum-compression packaging — is **technologically mature, fully open**, and well-documented in mass-production factory tours (e.g., the user-prompted source reference, foam pillow factory tour video `rsnSpo1O9fI`).\n\nThat methodology is **constitutionally neutral**: it underpins both extractive licensed-IP retail and a religious-corp first-party offering of plain, fully-disclosed, take-back-recyclable foam pillows. Without a dedicated actor:\n\n1. Religious-corp `kuni-umi` (planetary infra) does **not** cover consumer domestic textile goods; `tatekata` covers buildings; `yakushi` covers drugs. There is no first-party path to provide adherents with low-cost, fully-disclosed bedding articles.\n2. Adherents currently must purchase pillows from third parties that frequently contain undisclosed brominated/chlorinated fire-retardants (TDCPP / TCEP), undisclosed VOC off-gassing, licensed-IP markup, embedded RFID/IoT surveillance (Charter Rider §2(c)), or addictive-design fragrance impregnation.\n3. Foam pillow chemistry uses isocyanates (MDI / TDI) which are **OSHA-regulated respiratory sensitizers**. Gate-after-the-fact loses meaning; gates against TDI preference, against brominated FR chemistry, against IP licensing, against surveillance electronics, and against medical-device-class claims must be declared **before** capability lands — mirroring the wadachi / yakushi / tatekata / watatsumi R0 patterns.\n\nThis ADR fulfills that gap by reserving `makura` as a Tier-B actor, declaring 14 constitutional gates and 10 non-goals, and landing a 9-cell Pregel scaffold whose `solve()` methods raise `RuntimeError` until R1 activation.\n\nThe user-prompted source reference for this design is the manufacturing methodology survey in the YouTube video \"Inside a Massive Factory Making Millions of Foam Pillows\" (rsnSpo1O9fI, 2026). The methodology is adopted; the licensed-IP / surveillance / addictive-design retail layer is rejected per §2(b) + §2(c) + §1.13.\n\n## Decision\n\n### 1. Actor identity\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Actor name | `makura` |\n| Japanese | 枕 (basic domestic comfort article — sleep / rest as Wellbecoming foundation) |\n| Display name | `枕 (makura)` |\n| Tier (ADR-2605192415 §B) | **B** — per-domain leader, sibling of `kuni-umi` / `wadachi` / `tatekata` / `yakushi` / `watatsumi` / `mitsuho` / `hagukumi` |\n| Path-based DID | `did:web:etzhayyim.com:makura` |\n| Per-lot DID pattern (reserved) | `did:web:etzhayyim.com:makura:lot:<lotId>` |\n| Per-pillow DID pattern (reserved) | `did:web:etzhayyim.com:makura:pillow:<serial>` (R3 take-back recycling) |\n| Repo location | `20-actors/makura/` |\n| Lexicon namespace | `com.etzhayyim.makura.*` |\n| License | Apache 2.0 + Charter Compliance Rider v2.0 |\n\n### 2. Scope (R0)\n\n**In scope:**\n\n- Foam shred-fill pillows (PU foam crumb in woven cotton / recycled polyester shell)\n- Foam slab pillows (one-piece molded or cut-from-slabstock, no viscoelastic memory-foam in R0–R1)\n- Shell + closure assembly + dimensional/ILD QC + vacuum compression packaging\n- Take-back recycling chain (G13) — recycled crumb ≥10% in new fills by R3\n\n**Explicitly deferred to R2+ (separate ADR + Council Lv6+ supermajority):**\n\n- Memory-foam viscoelastic class (diisopropanolamine / dipropylene glycol chemistry uncertainty — N10)\n- Latex foam (Hevea / synthetic SBR) alternative — separate biome chemistry, separate ADR\n- Pillow protectors / pillow cases as separate SKU (R2+ — fabric-only line, no foam)\n\n**Constitutional non-goals (R0–R3, immutable; amendment requires Council Lv6+ supermajority + new ADR):** see §4 below.\n\n### 3. 5-Layer Foam-Pillow Assembly Process\n\nAdopted from mature global foam-pillow factory practice (slabstock + shredding + sewing + filling + packaging); civilianised / religious-corp-ised by disclosure, recycling, and surveillance / IP gates.\n\n| Layer | Stage | Key technology | Religious-corp constraints |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **L1** | 原料調達 (raw material attestation) | Polyol (polyether or polyester, bio-content % disclosed) + Isocyanate (MDI preferred — TDI requires Council attestation) + catalyst (DABCO / TEDA) + surfactant (silicone) + blowing agent (water + CO₂; HFC-only with Council attestation) | MDI preferred over TDI (worker exposure G6); no Hg / Sn-based catalysts; no HFC blowing agent without Council attestation; bio-polyol content disclosed |\n| **L2** | フォーム発泡 (foam blowing) | Slabstock one-shot or quasi-prepolymer process; conveyor belt; ~40-60 kg/m³ density; cell structure 30-80 ppi; cure 24-72 h | Closed-loop isocyanate dispensing (G6); VOC emission ≤ CertiPUR-US / OEKO-TEX Standard 100 equivalent (G7); no PBDE / TDCPP / TCEP / Sb₂O₃ FR chemistry (G8 + N5); each batch IPFS-pinned QC photo + density (G2) |\n| **L3** | 粉砕 / 切断 (shredding / cutting) | Mechanical shredding to crumb (8-15 mm typical) for shred-fill OR CNC profile cutting for slab pillows; particle distribution QA | Shredder dust collection + worker PPE; recycled crumb ≥10% blend by R3 (G13 take-back); no fragrance / oil impregnation at this stage (N7) |\n| **L4** | シェル縫製 (shell sewing) | Fabric attestation (organic cotton / recycled polyester preferred; print Charter Rider scan); three-side serge stitch shell; stitch density witness | Charter Rider §2(a-h) scan on every fabric print + label artwork (G5); no licensed IP / brand co-branding (N8); JP + EN bilingual care + material disclosure label (G4) |\n| **L5** | 充填 + 縫合 + QC + 包装 (fill + close + QC + pack) | Pneumatic crumb fill to spec weight ±2%; final stitch + label attach; dimensional + weight + ILD + visual QC; vacuum compression + carton + pallet | Witness quorum ≥2 distinct robots per pillow lot (Otete fill + Mimi QC) (G3); full BoM disclosure on every pillow tag (G12); take-back QR pinned to lot DID (G13); no embedded electronics / RFID beyond DID tag (G14 + N9) |\n\n### 4. Constitutional Gates (G1–G14, IMMUTABLE R0–R3)\n\n| Gate | Requirement | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| **G1** | All foam chemistry recipes (polyol formulation, catalyst, surfactant, blowing-agent ratios), shell-pattern CAD, and fill-line firmware **open-source** (Apache 2.0 + Charter Rider) | §2(b) anti-secrecy |\n| **G2** | Every foam batch + every pillow lot has **IPFS-pinned QC photo + density / ILD / dimensional record** (ADR-2605241500 dataset substrate) | Transparent material disclosure |\n| **G3** | Every pillow lot signed by **witness quorum ≥2 distinct robots** (Ed25519, DID-bound; Otete + Mimi pair canonical) | ADR-2605191524 swarm broadcast |\n| **G4** | All care instructions, material disclosure tags, and packaging text **JP + EN bilingual minimum** | §2(e) anti-gatekeeping of basic information |\n| **G5** | All fabric prints + label artwork pass **Charter Rider §2(a-h) scan** before release (no weapon imagery / no eschatology / no licensed IP) | §2(a) + §2(d) + §2(e) enforcement |\n| **G6** | Closed-loop isocyanate handling; worker exposure ≤ **5 ppb MDI** / ≤ **2 ppb TDI** 8h TWA (OSHA + NIOSH equivalent); MDI preferred over TDI | §1.13 worker wellbecoming + §2(g) chemical safety |\n| **G7** | VOC emission ≤ **CertiPUR-US / OEKO-TEX Standard 100** equivalent (formaldehyde ≤ 0.05 ppm; total VOC ≤ 0.5 mg/m³); 4-AB test panel | §1.13 indoor air wellbecoming + §2(g) |\n| **G8** | **No PBDE / TDCPP / TCEP / Sb₂O₃** fire-retardant chemistry; only graphite-FR or mineral-FR (ATH / Mg(OH)₂) when jurisdiction requires FR; baseline product is FR-free | §2(g) chemical safety; PBPK-toxic FR chemistry constitutionally prohibited |\n| **G9** | Inference paths (QC vision, defect classification, take-back image matching) use **Murakumo no-VKE mesh only** (ADR-2605214000 / ADR-2605215000) | Constitutional inference invariant |\n| **G10** | Isocyanate-dispense + foam-blowing + shredder + hot-stitch operations are **SBT-gated personnel**; non-SBT visitors require 1 SBT = 1 vote Council review | §1.13 worker wellbecoming + ADR-2605192315 Transparent Force personnel pattern |\n| **G11** | KPI caps: **max single-pillow foam mass 2.0 kg**; max dimensions **80 cm × 50 cm × 25 cm**; max single-shell mass 4.0 kg (foam + cover combined). No mattress-class or futon-class products (N1). Amendment requires Council Lv6+ supermajority | Prevent scope creep into ADR-2605261015 mitsuho-adjacent or future bedding actor |\n| **G12** | **Full BoM disclosure** on every pillow tag: polyol type + biocontent % / blowing agent / fabric blend (mass%) / fill weight / shred-vs-slab / fire-retardant disclosure (default \"none\") / country of origin / take-back QR | §2(e) anti-gatekeeping of material information |\n| **G13** | Every pillow has **IPFS-pinned take-back QR**; recycled foam crumb **≥10% mass blend** in new fills by R3 (community-scale); take-back center allocated by tatekata yard | Circular-material constitutional anchor (parallel to LandRegistry inalienability — pillow material returned to commons) |\n| **G14** | **No embedded sensors / no RFID / no NFC / no cooling-gel with PFAS / no smart-IoT** beyond the open-source DID paper-tag QR. Charter §2(c) anti-surveillance applied to consumer goods | §2(c) anti-surveillance |\n\n### 5. Non-Goals (N1–N10, IMMUTABLE R0–R3)\n\nCharter Rider §1.13 + §2(b) + §2(c) + §2(e) + §2(g) constitutional anchors:\n\n| ID | Excluded scope | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| **N1** | Mattresses + futons (full-size sleep surfaces, ≥ ILD class, ≥ size class beyond G11 caps) | Separate Tier-B actor if/when needed (G11 enforces) |\n| **N2** | Medical / clinical pressure-relief / decubitus prevention / orthopedic / pregnancy-pillow medical-device claims | Class I/II medical device regulatory gap (PMDA / FDA); yakushi-adjacent jurisdiction |\n| **N3** | CPAP-pillow / sleep-apnea / oxygen-mask integration | §2(h) medical-device, requires yakushi co-attestation |\n| **N4** | Mechanical adjustable / motorized / heated / cooled / smart-IoT pillows | §2(c) surveillance + §1.13 addictive-design + G14 |\n| **N5** | Brominated / chlorinated organophosphate fire-retardant chemistry (PBDE / TDCPP / TCEP / Sb₂O₃) | §2(g) PBPK-toxic; G8 constitutional |\n| **N6** | Down / feather / wool / silk animal-derived fill | Separate Tier-B for ethical animal-fiber sourcing if/when (ADR-pending); R0 plant-based + foam only |\n| **N7** | Aromatherapy / fragrance / essential-oil-impregnated foam | §1.13 addictive-design + indoor-air pollution; G7 violation |\n| **N8** | Licensed character / IP co-branding (Disney / Sanrio / sports leagues / etc.) | §2(b) IP-encumbrance + §2(e) anti-gatekeeping tier-pricing |\n| **N9** | Embedded electronics / sensors / RFID / NFC / cooling-gel-with-PFAS / phase-change-material with PFAS | §2(c) surveillance + §2(g) PFAS toxicity; G14 constitutional |\n| **N10** | Memory-foam viscoelastic class (diisopropanolamine / dipropylene glycol chemistry uncertainty) | Deferred to R2+ with Council Lv6+ review + dedicated ADR |\n\n### 6. 9 Pregel Cells + Murakumo Placement (R0 design-only)\n\n| Cell | Layer | Murakumo node | Phase |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `pillow_polyol_attestation` | L1a | naphtali | Polyol + catalyst + surfactant raw-material attestation (bio-content disclosed) |\n| `pillow_isocyanate_dispensing` | L1b | naphtali | Closed-loop MDI / TDI dispensing + worker exposure log (G6) |\n| `pillow_foam_blowing` | L2 | zebulun | Slabstock one-shot blowing; cell structure + density QA (G2 + G7) |\n| `pillow_foam_shredding` | L3 | joseph | Mechanical shredding to 8-15 mm crumb; particle distribution; recycled blend (G13) |\n| `pillow_fabric_attestation` | L4a | simeon | Fabric source + print Charter scan (G5); recycled poly / organic cotton preferred |\n| `pillow_shell_sewing` | L4b | dan | Three-side serge stitch shell assembly; Watari witness |\n| `pillow_filling_close` | L5a | dan | Pneumatic crumb fill ±2% + final stitch + bilingual label (G4 + G12) |\n| `pillow_qc` | L5b | levi | Dimensional + weight + ILD + visual defect (G2 + G3 Otete+Mimi witness) |\n| `pillow_packaging` | L5c | levi | Vacuum compression + carton + pallet + take-back QR pinning (G13) |\n\n### 7. Robotics Classes\n\n**New (R0 reservation only — physical builds blocked behind R1 ADR):**\n\n| Class | Role | Phase |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Watari (綿)** | Cotton / fabric handler for shell sewing + filling (3-axis gantry + needle-vision) | R1+ |\n| **Awa (泡)** | Foam slab / crumb handler for blowing line + shredder + pneumatic conveyance | R1+ |\n\n**Inherited (reuse, no marinization needed):**\n\n- Otete (kuni-umi manipulator) — chemical dispense + general handling\n- Mimi (kuni-umi metrology) — ILD + dimensional + weight QC + visual defect classification\n- Hitogata (kuni-umi humanoid) — R2+ for sewing finesse + label attach + sub-class C clean operations\n- Quad (kuni-umi logistics) — R2+ palletizing + carton handling\n\n### 8. Lexicon Namespace (8 record types, R0 stubs)\n\n```\ncom.etzhayyim.makura.{\n  foamBatchAttestation        # L2 — chemistry + density + cell-structure + VOC test\n  fabricAttestation           # L4a — material disclosure + Charter scan + dye safety\n  pillowLotAttestation        # L5a — fill weight + close + label + lot DID\n  qcRecord                    # L5b — dimensional + ILD + visual + reject %\n  packagingRecord             # L5c — vacuum compression + carton + pallet + take-back QR\n  recyclingCertificate        # G13 — take-back chain + recycled crumb % attestation\n  workerExposureRecord        # G6/G10 — isocyanate / VOC / dust exposure log\n  silenComfortReview          # Council 5-of-7 attestation, all new product classes\n}\n```\n\nSchema details deferred to R1 ADR.\n\n### 9. 4-Phase Roadmap\n\n| Phase | Scope | Trigger |\n|---|---|---|\n| **R0** (this wave) | Scaffold only; 9 cells RuntimeError; 8 lexicon stubs | ADR-2605261115 |\n| **R1** | Benchtop ≤1 kg foam batch blowing + 10-pillow lot QA; Watari prototype sewing; Awa prototype crumb-handling | ADR-2605261130 + Council Lv6+ + certified PU foam chemist SME + certified industrial hygienist SME |\n| **R2** | Pilot ≤100 pillows/day continuous slabstock + shredder + sewing + fill line; tatekata-shared shop allocation; first community-supply batch | ADR-2605261145 + 30-day public comment + take-back chain stand-up |\n| **R3** | Community-scale ≤5000 pillows/month + take-back recycling line operational (≥10% recycled crumb mass) + 60-day public review | ADR-2605261200 + 60-day public review + LANDS.md amendment if dedicated yard |\n\nReserved ADR slots: 2605261130 (R1), 2605261145 (R2), 2605261200 (R3).\n\n## Consequences\n\n**Positive:**\n\n- Adherents gain first-party access to fully-disclosed, take-back-recyclable foam pillows; no licensed-IP markup, no surveillance, no addictive-design fragrance, no toxic FR chemistry\n- Sleep / rest Wellbecoming domain (§1.13) gains its first dedicated manufacturing actor\n- Establishes the **circular-material constitutional pattern** (G13 take-back ≥10% recycled blend) that future consumer-goods Tier-B actors can adopt\n- Closed-loop isocyanate handling (G6) sets the worker-exposure precedent for future chemistry-touching actors\n- Charter Rider §2(c) anti-surveillance applied to a consumer good (G14 + N9) — first such application\n\n**Negative / risks:**\n\n- Isocyanate chemistry (even MDI preferred path) carries G6 worker-exposure risk; R1 activation gated on certified industrial hygienist SME onboarding\n- VOC off-gassing (G7) compliance requires expensive 4-AB test panel per batch — adds significant per-lot QA cost\n- Take-back recycling (G13 ≥10%) requires R3-scale logistics chain not yet in place; risk of R3 slip\n- Without N8 licensed-IP carve-out, makura pillows will look visually plain — risk of low community uptake (mitigated: this is constitutional, not market-fit-driven)\n- N6 down/feather exclusion narrows fill chemistry to PU + future latex/cotton/recycled only — risk of unmet adherent preference for traditional fills\n\n**Mitigation:**\n\n- R1 ADR gates SME onboarding (certified PU foam chemist + certified industrial hygienist) before any physical chemistry\n- VOC test cost reduced over time via Mimi-class metrology in-line sensor R2+\n- Take-back logistics piggyback tatekata yard + kuni-umi Quad fleet (no dedicated CAPEX in R0–R2)\n- N6 animal-fill carve-out reserved for future actor with proper ethical sourcing constitutional review\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n1. **Sub-cell of kuni-umi rather than dedicated Tier-B actor** — rejected: kuni-umi scope is planetary infrastructure (utilities, structures, agriculture in mitsuho sibling), not consumer domestic goods. Confused responsibility surface; foam pillow chemistry + textile sewing has no overlap with kuni-umi's S-stages.\n2. **Bundle with future bedding actor (mattress + sheet + pillow + futon as one Tier-B)** — rejected: scope too large for R0; mattress class would trigger entirely different metallurgy (innerspring) or much higher foam mass with different blowing chemistry; futon class triggers different fill chemistry (cotton / wool / silk). G11 KPI caps explicitly prevent this drift.\n3. **Allow licensed IP co-branding (rejected N8)** — rejected: §2(b) IP-encumbrance + §2(e) anti-gatekeeping tier-pricing. Constitutional non-goal.\n4. **Allow embedded sleep-tracking electronics (rejected N9 + G14)** — rejected: §2(c) anti-surveillance constitutional anchor.\n5. **Allow brominated FR chemistry (rejected N5 + G8)** — rejected: §2(g) PBPK-toxic FR chemistry constitutionally prohibited; graphite-FR + mineral-FR (ATH / Mg(OH)₂) sufficient when jurisdiction requires FR; baseline FR-free.\n6. **Allow memory-foam viscoelastic in R0 (rejected N10)** — rejected: diisopropanolamine / dipropylene glycol chemistry uncertainty; deferred to R2+ with Council Lv6+ review + dedicated ADR.\n7. **Latex foam alternative in R0** — rejected: Hevea latex biome chemistry + SBR alternative require entirely different sourcing + curing + ILD characterization; future R2+ ADR.\n\n## References\n\n- Source video methodology: YouTube `rsnSpo1O9fI` \"Inside a Massive Factory Making Millions of Foam Pillows\" (2026; manufacturing methodology adopted; licensed-IP / surveillance / addictive-design retail layer rejected per §2(b) + §2(c) + §1.13)\n- ADR-2605192100 — etzhayyim mission charter (§1.13 Wellbecoming, §2(e) anti-gatekeeping)\n- ADR-2605192200 — Charter Rider v2.0 (§2(a-h) prohibited categories)\n- ADR-2605192400 — Eros / Gore content policy\n- ADR-2605192415 — religious-corp daemon architecture (Tier-B definition)\n- ADR-2605201400 — kuni-umi planetary infra fleet (sibling)\n- ADR-2605242000 — wadachi autonomous mobility R0 (sibling pattern)\n- ADR-2605250500 — yakushi pharmaceutical R0 (sibling pattern; chemistry-handling precedent)\n- ADR-2605250715 — tatekata construction R0 (sibling pattern; yard-sharing for R2 pilot)\n- ADR-2605252200 — watatsumi civilian submersible R0 (sibling pattern; 14-gate / non-goal structure mirrored)\n- ADR-2605261015 — mitsuho food / agriculture R0 (sibling pattern; consumer-goods Tier-B precedent)\n- ADR-2605261030 — hagukumi care R0 (sibling pattern)\n- ADR-2605214000 — Murakumo no-VKE mesh + lexicon port rules\n- ADR-2605215000 — etzhayyim inference Murakumo-fleet-only\n- ADR-2605191524 — Transparent Force swarm broadcast witness quorum\n- ADR-2605241500 — etzhayyim dataset CID substrate (IPFS-pinned QC evidence)\n- /CHARTER-RIDER.md — license addendum canonical text\n- 20-actors/makura/README.edn — actor scaffold\n- 20-actors/makura/manifest.jsonld — actor manifest (DID + cell registry + gates + non-goals)\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2605261115-makura-foam-pillow-tier-b-actor-r0.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "makura-foam-pillow-r0", :adr/last_verified "2026-05-25", :adr/date "2026-05-25", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/related ["wellbecoming-karma-lean-proofs" "wellbecoming-karma-lean-proofs" "wellbecoming-karma-lean-proofs" "wellbecoming-karma-lean-proofs" "wellbecoming-karma-lean-proofs"], :adr/authoritative_for ["makura actor identity (name, DID, tier, namespace, scope boundary) — R0 reservation" "foam-pillow manufacturing constitutional gates (G1..G14) and non-goals (N1..N10)" "R0 → R3 phased roadmap with R1/R2/R3 ADR reservation" "5-layer foam-pillow assembly process (raw-material → foam-blowing → shredding → shell-sewing → fill-close-QC-pack)" "9 Pregel cell catalog + Murakumo placement (R0 design-only)" "2 new robotics class reservation (Watari 綿 / Awa 泡) + 4 inherited reuse (Otete / Mimi / Hitogata / Quad)" "lexicon namespace reservation (`com.etzhayyim.makura.*`, 8 record types)"]}]
